    <category name="dotnet" class="csonly">
        
        <p>SaxonCS adds support for LINQ documents (<code>XDocument</code> class) alongside DOM support. The <code>DocumentBuilder</code>
        has new methods to allow building from a LINQ source, or wrapping a LINQ node as an XDM node, and a new <code>LinqDestination</code>
        class allows the result of a query or transformation to be written to a LINQ tree.</p>
        
        <p>With this feature, it becomes possible to run XPath 3.1 queries against LINQ documents, returning nodes in the original LINQ 
            tree.</p>
        
        
